  "verbalization": "Hydrocortisone is implicated in the pathogenesis of Non-histaminic Angioedema through a chain of indications that link it to Triamcinolone, which in turn is associated with the condition. The evidence suggests that Hydrocortisone may act as a precursor in the development of Non-histaminic Angioedema, possibly through indirect mechanisms involving inflammation or immune modulation. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Hydrocortisone to Non-histaminic Angioedema highlights a potential role in the broader context of inflammatory or immunological processes. While the direct causal link remains unclear, the cumulative evidence points to a possible dependency on corticosteroids, such as Hydrocortisone, in the manifestation of this condition. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of corticosteroids in the pathophysiology of Non-histaminic Angioedema, though further research is needed to elucidate the precise mechanisms.",
